use ../lib/CodingRule

from ./CertJava import CertJava

export coding-rule CertJavaLck00J:
    standard: @{CertJava}
    ruleId: LCK00-J
    title: Use private final lock objects to synchronize classes that may interact with untrusted code
    statement:
        When a class can be reached by untrusted code, guard its state with
        a private final lock object and synchronized blocks, not with
        synchronized methods or a lock that callers can see or replace.
    rationale:
        Synchronized methods lock on this, which any caller can also lock
        and hold forever. An attacker who holds that lock, or swaps a public
        lock field, can block every other thread and cause a denial of
        service. CERT's risk assessment gives likelihood probable,
        detectable no, repairable no, priority P2 and level L3.
    exceptions:
        A class may break the rule if it documents that its objects must not
        reach untrusted code, it does not call into untrusted classes that
        break the rule, and its synchronization policy is documented.
        Clients may use such a class under the same conditions.
    severity: low
    noncompliant:
        ```java
        \\\
        public class Account {
            private long balance;

            public synchronized void deposit(long amount) {
                balance += amount;
            }
        }
        \\\
        ```
    compliant:
        ```java
        \\\
        public class Account {
            private final Object lock = new Object();
            private long balance;

            public void deposit(long amount) {
                synchronized (lock) {
                    balance += amount;
                }
            }
        }
        \\\
        ```
    languages: [java]
    tags: [concurrency, locking, denial-of-service]
    source: https://cmu-sei.github.io/secure-coding-standards/sei-cert-oracle-coding-standard-for-java/rules/locking-lck/lck00-j/
